# Pins the dav1d build the Windows test job prebuilds, sourced by
# `.github/workflows/ci.yml`'s `Build dav1d (Windows)` step:
#
#   cd "$GITHUB_WORKSPACE"
#   set -a; . ./scripts/ci-pins.env; set +a
#
# A file of its own rather than two lines inline in ci.yml because the weekly
# bump (`.github/workflows/appimage-bump.yml` -> `scripts/bump-appimage.sh`)
# must be able to move these values, and a push that creates or modifies a file
# under `.github/workflows/` requires the `workflows` permission, which
# `GITHUB_TOKEN` can never hold. `scripts/bump-appimage.sh` rewrites the two
# values below (`--apply`, one pass, temp file + mv) and owns the `dav1d-ci`
# row of its report; nothing else writes this file.
#
# `DAV1D_TAG` is a dav1d release tag. `DAV1D_COMMIT` is that tag's *peeled*
# commit, never the tag object: ci.yml fetches
# `https://github.com/videolan/dav1d/archive/$DAV1D_COMMIT.tar.gz`, and an
# archive URL for an annotated tag's own sha is a 404. The step asserts the
# unpacked meson.build carries `version: '$DAV1D_TAG'`, so the two values only
# make sense together. Keep each value on its own unquoted line; trailing text
# after a value is preserved by the bump, and `#` starts a comment.
DAV1D_TAG=1.5.5
DAV1D_COMMIT=6c7bee685677fd997a431302be4fea8ea4017606
